      "name": "md-slides",
      "path": "markdown-html/skills/md-slides",
      "description": "Converts a markdown deck (slides separated by `---` HR boundaries or by `# ` H1 headings, with optional HTML-comment `notes:` presenter-notes blocks) into a single-file HTML presentation with arrow-key / space / PgDn / PgUp / Home / End / P / Esc keyboard navigation, presenter mode (split view with current slide + speaker notes + clock + next-slide preview), URL-hash deep linking, and `@media print` page-per-slide for PDF export. Triggers when the markdown-html-orchestrator classifies an input as SLIDES, or when invoked directly via /cs-md-slides. Reuses md-document's markdown parser for \u2026",
